{
  "$comment": "Every engine feature exists twice, in C# under SexyBiscuit.Engine and in JavaScript under html5/src. This map names each twin. mirror-check.js fails a change that touches one side of a strict pair and not the other; the parity tests on both sides walk the pairs whose check is 'schema' (every JS static-schema key is a C# property) or 'names' (an enum's member set). 'tables' are the JSON files both engines read; the C# csproj embeds them. components.csOnly and jsOnly list what exists on one engine on purpose; the sweep tests fail on anything registered that is in neither the pairs nor those lists. Look a twin up with: node html5/tools/mirror-check.js --of <file>.",
